      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:18:7",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا أَذَّنْتَ فَأَفْصِحْ بِالْأَلِفِ وَ الْهَاءِ وَ صَلِّ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ كُلَّمَا ذَكَرْتَهُ أَوْ ذَكَرَهُ ذَاكِرٌ فِي أَذَانٍ وَ غَيْرِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Hammad Bin Isa, from Hareyz, from Zurara who said, ",
          "‘Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When you recite the <span class=\"iTxt\">Azān</span>, so be eloquent with the ‘Alif’ and the ‘Ha’ (two letters of the Arabic Alphabet), and send Blessings upon the Prophet<sup>saww</sup> every time you mention it, or a mentioner mentions it during an <span class=\"iTxt\">Azān</span> or an <span class=\"iTxt\">Iqamah</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from Hammad ibn ‘Isa from Hariz from Zurarah who has said the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘When you say Adhan say Alif and al-Ha’ (two letters of Arabic alphabet) clearly and say O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause whenever you mention his name or someone else mentions his name in Adhan or in other expressions.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
